# MAGIC
# MAGIC ##### Additional notes
# MAGIC
# MAGIC <details>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - This is a high-level overview of integrating GitFlow (a branching model using feature branches and multiple primary branches) with DABs, using GitHub Actions for automation.
# MAGIC - A developer creates a feature branch from dev, where features or bug fixes are developed in isolation, and can deploy directly to the DEV workspace using the Databricks CLI.
# MAGIC - Once a feature is complete, a pull request is opened; after peer review, it is merged into dev.
# MAGIC - Merging into dev triggers a GitHub Actions workflow that deploys to the QA environment using DABs, runs tests, code coverage, and security scans, creates a release branch, and opens a PR to main.
# MAGIC - After the release PR is closed, another workflow deploys the bundle to prod, creates a release tag, and opens a PR from main back to dev.
# MAGIC - Critical production issues are handled with a hotfix branch from main, merged back into both main and dev after the fix &mdash; keeping production stable while development continues.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC </details>

