# MAGIC ### C1. Overview of Git with Databricks
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Git is a free, open-source framework for tracking source-code changes during software development. You can integrate third-party Git tools and services that fit your organization's needs.
# MAGIC <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;font-family:sans-serif;"><span style="background:rgba(255,95,70,0.08);border:1px solid #4299E0;border-radius:16px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:14pt;color:#0b2026;">GitHub</span><span style="background:rgba(255,95,70,0.08);border:1px solid #4299E0;border-radius:16px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:14pt;color:#0b2026;">GitHub Actions</span><span style="background:rgba(255,95,70,0.08);border:1px solid #4299E0;border-radius:16px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:14pt;color:#0b2026;">GitLab</span><span style="background:rgba(255,95,70,0.08);border:1px solid #4299E0;border-radius:16px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:14pt;color:#0b2026;">Azure DevOps</span><span style="background:rgba(255,95,70,0.08);border:1px solid #4299E0;border-radius:16px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:14pt;color:#0b2026;">Bitbucket</span></div>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ##### Additional notes
# MAGIC
